1
00:00:07,060 --> 00:00:09,563
Yah-hoo!

2
00:00:09,646 --> 00:00:12,065
-Yay! Yay! Yay! Yay!
-Hey.

3
00:00:12,149 --> 00:00:13,567
-Woo-hoo. Woo-hoo.
-Um…

4
00:00:14,067 --> 00:00:14,943
Your friend?

5
00:00:15,569 --> 00:00:16,903
Great question.

6
00:00:16,987 --> 00:00:19,906
The name's Junta Hayami,
we're childhood friends.

7
00:00:20,824 --> 00:00:22,993
Did-- Did you sleep here?

8
00:00:23,076 --> 00:00:26,538
This is my friend, Kazuki. Funny story,
he has a string of back luck,

9
00:00:26,621 --> 00:00:28,999
so he's gonna be crashing here
at my place for now.

10
00:00:29,791 --> 00:00:32,002
He's… crashing here?

11
00:00:32,085 --> 00:00:34,337
Yeah, it's a really long story.

12
00:00:34,421 --> 00:00:36,339
I'm just gonna go.

13
00:00:36,423 --> 00:00:37,257
Yeah. Sure.

14
00:00:37,758 --> 00:00:39,676
I forgot my bag.

15
00:00:42,095 --> 00:00:43,055
Hmm.

16
00:00:48,143 --> 00:00:49,102
He's tall.

17
00:00:49,603 --> 00:00:51,188
He's really good-looking.

18
00:02:23,238 --> 00:02:25,991
#4 THE CHILDHOOD FRIEND IS EASY MODE

19
00:02:26,074 --> 00:02:27,117
A victory!

20
00:02:33,707 --> 00:02:36,501
-Hey! Explain yourself, you devil!
-Wait! I'm Riri!

21
00:02:36,585 --> 00:02:39,129
Your helpful wizard friend, not the devil!

22
00:02:40,422 --> 00:02:41,756
You're no friend of mine.

23
00:02:41,840 --> 00:02:46,011
And what's with that guy out there?
He keeps saying we're childhood friends.

24
00:02:46,094 --> 00:02:48,513
Reuniting with a childhood friend.

25
00:02:48,597 --> 00:02:51,016
Another classic romance scenario.

26
00:02:51,099 --> 00:02:52,475
ROMANTIC THRILLER

27
00:02:52,559 --> 00:02:55,937
The two of you grew up together.
You were inseparable.

28
00:02:56,021 --> 00:03:01,026
Before you know it, those feelings
of friendship turned into sparks of love.

29
00:03:01,109 --> 00:03:02,527
-…the problem here.
-Let me take a look at it.

30
00:03:03,361 --> 00:03:07,282
What? I don't remember having a friend
like that, especially one that's so cute.

31
00:03:07,866 --> 00:03:10,202
Well, his name is Junta Hayami.

32
00:03:10,285 --> 00:03:12,996
And you've been besties
since elementary school.

33
00:03:13,079 --> 00:03:14,789
But it's a lie. It's not true!

34
00:03:15,790 --> 00:03:19,169
Junta's the hottest rookie
on the school's baseball team this year.

35
00:03:19,252 --> 00:03:21,296
After being separated
for three long years,

36
00:03:21,379 --> 00:03:23,048
you've been reunited.

37
00:03:23,131 --> 00:03:25,050
That's an oddly specific backstory.

38
00:03:25,133 --> 00:03:27,302
I haven't even told you the best part yet.

39
00:03:27,886 --> 00:03:32,057
Junta's had a secret crush on you
since elementary school!

40
00:03:32,140 --> 00:03:33,558
Don't do this to him!

41
00:03:33,642 --> 00:03:38,313
Do you get it? All you have to do
to win the game is accept his feelings.

42
00:03:38,396 --> 00:03:42,400
I call it Easy Mode in Romantic Thriller.

43
00:03:42,484 --> 00:03:44,319
You call this "Easy Mode"!

44
00:03:44,402 --> 00:03:46,404
Just go away, devil.

45
00:03:46,905 --> 00:03:48,448
Now, begone, evil spirit!

46
00:03:48,531 --> 00:03:51,326
I've already told you
I'm not the devil or an evil spirit.

47
00:03:52,285 --> 00:03:54,746
How did I end up
in such a ridiculous spot?

48
00:03:54,829 --> 00:03:57,916
When you think about it,
it's not all that ridiculous.

49
00:03:57,999 --> 00:04:01,670
Having a crush on your best friend
is a classic scenario.

50
00:04:01,753 --> 00:04:04,130
Hey, stop putting
these dumb thoughts into my head.

51
00:04:04,214 --> 00:04:05,840
You're cute when you're embarrassed.

52
00:04:05,924 --> 00:04:07,550
Who you're calling cute?

53
00:04:09,636 --> 00:04:12,639
Crap, what was his name? Jun… Jo…

54
00:04:12,722 --> 00:04:14,057
You mean Junta?

55
00:04:14,641 --> 00:04:18,061
Yeah, he's been out there
for a while now, hasn't he?

56
00:04:18,144 --> 00:04:21,064
Oh, don't worry. I took care of that.

57
00:04:21,147 --> 00:04:26,069
He's in his own scenario, see? He's been
chatting with you this whole time.

58
00:04:26,903 --> 00:04:28,571
-Kirarin!
-Uh, sorry.

59
00:04:29,155 --> 00:04:32,075
I'm not all that familiar
with torture methods.

60
00:04:32,158 --> 00:04:34,452
What the hell
were we talking about?

61
00:04:37,038 --> 00:04:40,417
I got to say I was surprised earlier.

62
00:04:41,084 --> 00:04:44,087
I swear I don't usually
talk about torture.

63
00:04:44,170 --> 00:04:45,630
It wasn't about that.

64
00:04:47,215 --> 00:04:48,800
It was Kazuki.

65
00:04:49,467 --> 00:04:51,261
Kazuki? What about him?

66
00:04:51,344 --> 00:04:53,346
Look, I think it's great
that you're helping a friend

67
00:04:53,430 --> 00:04:55,140
out of a bad situation,

68
00:04:55,223 --> 00:04:57,392
but it's rude of him
to put you out like that.

69
00:04:57,976 --> 00:05:02,022
Put me out? Nah, doesn't bother me.
The room was empty, anyway.

70
00:05:02,814 --> 00:05:05,775
Right, but… you sure it's a good idea?

71
00:05:05,859 --> 00:05:07,902
I mean, how well do you really know him?

72
00:05:07,986 --> 00:05:11,531
Seriously, I know a lot more
about him than I do about you.

73
00:05:12,240 --> 00:05:16,661
No worries. Kazuki's not great
at first impressions, but he's a good guy.

74
00:05:16,745 --> 00:05:20,540
Besides, he's got so many fangirls,
he's totally over the whole scene.

75
00:05:21,624 --> 00:05:23,710
I see, well, okay.

76
00:05:23,793 --> 00:05:26,296
I guess if your parents were cool
with him staying at your place,

77
00:05:26,379 --> 00:05:28,673
then I shouldn't be
too worried about it, either.

78
00:05:29,257 --> 00:05:31,384
Maybe you should try
worrying less about him

79
00:05:31,468 --> 00:05:33,261
and worrying more
about yourself there, buddy.

80
00:05:33,345 --> 00:05:34,679
MIND CONTROL BY THE DEVIL

81
00:05:34,763 --> 00:05:37,474
This whole thing is my fault.

82
00:05:37,557 --> 00:05:38,391
What?

83
00:05:38,475 --> 00:05:40,185
Uh, nothing, really.

84
00:05:42,771 --> 00:05:45,065
Hey, what's going on in here?

85
00:05:45,148 --> 00:05:46,941
-This wind is so strong.
-Are you okay?

86
00:05:48,360 --> 00:05:49,319
Yeah.

87
00:05:49,402 --> 00:05:50,612
-Anzu.
-Huh?

88
00:05:53,865 --> 00:05:55,200
H-- Hey…

89
00:05:56,576 --> 00:05:57,702
Just hold still.

90
00:06:00,163 --> 00:06:01,206
You've got…

91
00:06:01,289 --> 00:06:03,708
a Hercules beetle stuck in your hair.

92
00:06:04,793 --> 00:06:05,710
What?

93
00:06:05,794 --> 00:06:07,796
What the…

94
00:06:07,879 --> 00:06:10,298
What is that thing? It's freaking huge!

95
00:06:10,382 --> 00:06:12,384
-Quit squirming.
-Ah, no, no, no, no. Ah!

96
00:06:12,467 --> 00:06:15,720
-Oh, it's really tangled in there.
-Hurry up! Get it off me!

97
00:06:18,306 --> 00:06:19,224
Ta-da!

98
00:06:19,307 --> 00:06:21,226
SINCE IT IS UNSIGHTLY,
WE'VE CONVERTED IT TO A CREPE.

99
00:06:22,185 --> 00:06:23,728
Oh, gross! Get it away from me!

100
00:06:23,812 --> 00:06:25,855
-Get rid of that thing!
-Uh, uh…

101
00:06:25,939 --> 00:06:26,940
My bad. Sorry.

102
00:06:28,274 --> 00:06:30,068
Look how big this one is.

103
00:06:30,151 --> 00:06:32,320
I'll bet you it's worth
at least a hundred dollars.

104
00:06:32,404 --> 00:06:36,574
One hundred?
That ugly beetle's worth that much?

105
00:06:40,453 --> 00:06:41,871
Stop it!

106
00:06:41,955 --> 00:06:42,956
Catch it!

107
00:06:43,456 --> 00:06:45,375
I think I can still reach it.

108
00:06:45,458 --> 00:06:46,376
Incoming!

109
00:06:47,043 --> 00:06:47,877
It's gonna hurt.

110
00:06:49,462 --> 00:06:51,381
Anzu!

111
00:06:58,847 --> 00:07:00,723
I… got you.

112
00:07:03,560 --> 00:07:06,646
Um, nice catch. Great reflexes.

113
00:07:07,397 --> 00:07:10,108
Oh, thanks. Just glad you're okay.

114
00:07:11,860 --> 00:07:14,195
Ugh, damn it, Junta.
Why do you have to be such a great guy?

115
00:07:14,279 --> 00:07:15,155
Uh…

116
00:07:15,738 --> 00:07:16,698
What?

117
00:07:17,282 --> 00:07:20,535
It's just that beetle
really messed up your hair.

118
00:07:20,618 --> 00:07:22,662
What? My hair?

119
00:07:24,706 --> 00:07:25,790
You want me to fix it?

120
00:07:26,583 --> 00:07:27,459
Um…

121
00:07:28,585 --> 00:07:29,461
Could you?

122
00:07:32,172 --> 00:07:34,424
You know,
I remember in elementary school,

123
00:07:34,507 --> 00:07:36,885
the kids used to call you
"Frizzy" and "Annie"

124
00:07:36,968 --> 00:07:39,053
because your hair was so red and curly.

125
00:07:39,637 --> 00:07:41,973
They implanted
that memory, too. Devil!

126
00:07:42,640 --> 00:07:43,766
I remember.

127
00:07:44,350 --> 00:07:45,977
Ryuya and his friends used to call me that

128
00:07:46,060 --> 00:07:48,021
because I constantly beat them at games.

129
00:07:49,772 --> 00:07:52,942
Hey, what was that one video game
you used to play all the time?

130
00:07:53,026 --> 00:07:54,360
Cat Ranger?

131
00:07:54,444 --> 00:07:57,697
Yes! Cat Ranger! Oh, that was classic.

132
00:07:57,780 --> 00:08:00,909
It was such an obscure game,
but it was so much fun to play.

133
00:08:00,992 --> 00:08:03,912
So, what sort of games
are you playing now?

134
00:08:04,496 --> 00:08:07,790
Well, recently, they were all confiscated.

135
00:08:07,874 --> 00:08:09,417
Huh? But what happened?

136
00:08:09,501 --> 00:08:11,794
I keep asking myself
the same thing!

137
00:08:12,879 --> 00:08:14,506
How is it going back there?

138
00:08:14,589 --> 00:08:17,509
Uh, sorry, guess I'm not
so good with my hands.

139
00:08:17,592 --> 00:08:18,801
Not good with his hands?

140
00:08:18,885 --> 00:08:20,178
-Anzu!
-Huh!

141
00:08:20,929 --> 00:08:22,013
Good morning.

142
00:08:22,096 --> 00:08:23,765
Hey! Morning, Saki.

143
00:08:23,848 --> 00:08:25,558
Hi, Junta. How are you?

144
00:08:25,642 --> 00:08:26,684
Morning.

145
00:08:26,768 --> 00:08:28,645
Saki knows Junta?

146
00:08:28,728 --> 00:08:31,523
That little devil got to her, too!

147
00:08:32,690 --> 00:08:35,443
Anzu, do you want me
to help you with your hair?

148
00:08:35,527 --> 00:08:36,653
You wouldn't mind?

149
00:08:36,736 --> 00:08:38,071
That would be great.

150
00:08:40,949 --> 00:08:42,575
There. Perfect.

151
00:08:42,659 --> 00:08:44,202
You're the best.

152
00:08:44,285 --> 00:08:47,789
You know what? You should start
wearing scrunchies. You look so cute.

153
00:08:49,082 --> 00:08:50,375
Junta, your thoughts?

154
00:08:50,458 --> 00:08:51,292
Me?

155
00:08:53,127 --> 00:08:54,045
Yeah.

156
00:08:55,255 --> 00:08:58,174
What's with that face?

157
00:08:59,050 --> 00:09:00,218
Oh, thanks.

158
00:09:00,802 --> 00:09:03,179
She totally asked him on purpose.

159
00:09:05,348 --> 00:09:09,686
Well, Junta's actually a really nice guy.
I wasn't sure what to expect

160
00:09:09,769 --> 00:09:13,481
from my mysterious childhood friend
showing up out of the blue,

161
00:09:13,565 --> 00:09:15,692
but it's kinda weird how comfortable it is

162
00:09:15,775 --> 00:09:18,695
-just hanging out with him and Saki.
-She screams so loud.

163
00:09:18,778 --> 00:09:20,863
It almost feels like
we really are old friends.

164
00:09:27,787 --> 00:09:29,247
-Tsukasa.
-Hm?

165
00:09:29,789 --> 00:09:32,709
Morning. Happy to see
you're heading back to school today.

166
00:09:32,792 --> 00:09:34,460
Whoa, did you get a new phone?

167
00:09:35,169 --> 00:09:37,630
Yeah, can't do anything
without one, so…

168
00:09:38,339 --> 00:09:39,841
-Tsukasa!
-Huh?

169
00:09:41,217 --> 00:09:44,637
I can't believe
you just abandoned us like that yesterday.

170
00:09:45,263 --> 00:09:47,849
And to make it worse,
you totally ditched us

171
00:09:47,932 --> 00:09:50,393
for a girl from another class.

172
00:09:50,476 --> 00:09:53,021
Wait! Were you really with a girl?

173
00:09:53,104 --> 00:09:54,606
That's different.

174
00:09:54,689 --> 00:09:56,274
Trust me. She's just a friend.

175
00:09:56,858 --> 00:09:58,860
You got a new phone?

176
00:09:59,360 --> 00:10:01,571
Here, let's exchange our numbers.

177
00:10:02,614 --> 00:10:04,282
-I think I'll pass.
-What--

178
00:10:04,365 --> 00:10:07,410
And find someone else to follow around.

179
00:10:09,370 --> 00:10:11,706
No way! Meanie.

180
00:10:12,290 --> 00:10:14,667
Would it kill you to be a little nicer?

181
00:10:14,751 --> 00:10:16,753
If I'm not plunged, she won't learn.

182
00:10:16,836 --> 00:10:18,546
Oh, let me get your number.

183
00:10:19,130 --> 00:10:21,341
You're really gonna call?

184
00:10:25,762 --> 00:10:30,350
Whose bright idea was it
to put PE before lunch? I'm starving!

185
00:10:30,933 --> 00:10:33,478
Same. Looking forward
to a home-cooked lunch.

186
00:10:33,561 --> 00:10:35,855
-You always cook for yourself?
-Yeah.

187
00:10:36,522 --> 00:10:38,399
Well,
since you're already making food,

188
00:10:38,483 --> 00:10:40,610
how about you make a little extra for me?

189
00:10:40,693 --> 00:10:42,820
-No.
-Doesn't hurt to ask.

190
00:10:43,404 --> 00:10:45,406
I'm already making two lunches.

191
00:10:45,907 --> 00:10:47,450
There's a quiz in Math.

192
00:10:49,619 --> 00:10:50,453
Hello.

193
00:10:51,162 --> 00:10:52,038
Hm.

194
00:10:53,539 --> 00:10:55,958
Hold up. Do you really know Junta Hayami?

195
00:10:56,042 --> 00:10:56,959
Do you know him?

196
00:10:57,543 --> 00:11:00,338
Only the star rookie
of our baseball team this year.

197
00:11:00,421 --> 00:11:02,715
There are rumors that he'll even go pro.

198
00:11:03,341 --> 00:11:06,844
I didn't realize Hoshino
had such a popular childhood friend.

199
00:11:07,428 --> 00:11:09,430
How could you not have heard of him?

200
00:11:09,514 --> 00:11:13,101
He's out on the field practicing
almost every free period there is.

201
00:11:13,726 --> 00:11:15,645
Plus, he's tall and good-looking, too.

202
00:11:16,646 --> 00:11:18,981
Don't be jealous.
You're just as good-looking.

203
00:11:20,608 --> 00:11:22,860
I am not jealous of that guy.

204
00:11:22,944 --> 00:11:24,862
-Did you stand us up? Hey.
-Man!

205
00:11:24,946 --> 00:11:26,906
He's gonna be crashing here
at my place for now.

206
00:11:26,989 --> 00:11:29,325
He's… crashing here?

207
00:11:29,909 --> 00:11:32,245
You said you don't wanna date
anyone right now, right?

208
00:11:32,328 --> 00:11:34,247
Oh, great! 'Cause me, too.

209
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:39,210
Yeah, we'll see.

210
00:11:42,088 --> 00:11:47,176
So, hey, what do you guys know
about that guy? His name is Kazuki.

211
00:11:47,260 --> 00:11:48,344
Oh, I thought you knew him.

212
00:11:48,428 --> 00:11:50,513
No, I just met him this morning.

213
00:11:51,097 --> 00:11:53,099
I've heard of him.
I think he's in Class 7.

214
00:11:53,182 --> 00:11:55,643
I always hear the girls
whispering about him.

215
00:11:55,727 --> 00:11:57,645
So he's pretty popular then.

216
00:11:57,729 --> 00:11:59,522
What? Does that make him your enemy?

217
00:12:00,106 --> 00:12:04,610
He's popular and smart.
He's placed top ten in the midterms.

218
00:12:04,694 --> 00:12:05,528
Top ten?

219
00:12:06,237 --> 00:12:08,114
That guy's
on a whole different level.

220
00:12:08,197 --> 00:12:09,407
Agreed.

221
00:12:09,949 --> 00:12:12,034
What's with this
slow march down the hall?

222
00:12:12,118 --> 00:12:13,202
Mind if we join?

223
00:12:13,745 --> 00:12:15,705
Oh, hey, guys, look who it is.

224
00:12:15,788 --> 00:12:16,622
Hm.

225
00:12:17,915 --> 00:12:20,251
Do either of you know Tsukasa Kazuki?

226
00:12:21,002 --> 00:12:24,338
Kazuki? You mean
the really hot from Class 7?

227
00:12:24,422 --> 00:12:26,215
Did you know he's friends with Junta?

228
00:12:26,299 --> 00:12:27,300
Jealous!

229
00:12:27,383 --> 00:12:29,051
Well, more like a friend of a friend.

230
00:12:29,761 --> 00:12:33,473
Uh, question. If he asked to,
I don't know, sleepover at your place,

231
00:12:33,556 --> 00:12:34,557
would you guys let him?

232
00:12:34,640 --> 00:12:37,560
-Oh, my gosh. Yes, of course, I would.
-Mm-hm.

233
00:12:38,144 --> 00:12:41,063
Then we fall in love
and live happily ever after.

234
00:12:41,647 --> 00:12:42,690
I figured.

235
00:12:42,774 --> 00:12:44,776
What's up?
You're just as popular as him.

236
00:12:44,859 --> 00:12:46,068
-Hell yeah.
-Hell yeah.

237
00:12:46,152 --> 00:12:50,490
Don't deny it, we all saw you flirting
with that cute girl you grew up with.

238
00:12:50,573 --> 00:12:51,949
You even walked her to school.

239
00:12:53,159 --> 00:12:57,663
Flirt? No, Anzu's just an old friend.
That's all it is, though…

240
00:12:57,747 --> 00:12:59,248
"Though"? Though what?

241
00:12:59,332 --> 00:13:01,584
I mean… Never mind.

242
00:13:03,085 --> 00:13:05,421
They're right, though.
Anzu is really cute.

243
00:13:05,505 --> 00:13:07,173
Her hair, her smile…

244
00:13:07,673 --> 00:13:09,967
No, I can't be thinking this stuff!

245
00:13:10,051 --> 00:13:12,804
Hey, uh, is that really helping anything?

246
00:13:18,392 --> 00:13:19,936
I'm sorry, Anzu.

247
00:13:20,436 --> 00:13:22,730
I've got a broadcast club meeting
during lunch today.

248
00:13:23,397 --> 00:13:25,817
Yeah, um-hm, it's all good.

249
00:13:26,984 --> 00:13:28,110
Bye!

250
00:13:28,194 --> 00:13:30,696
It's really him,
the hottest boy in Class 7.

251
00:13:31,989 --> 00:13:32,824
Hoshino.

252
00:13:33,449 --> 00:13:34,283
Hm?

253
00:13:35,326 --> 00:13:36,285
Come here.

254
00:13:37,453 --> 00:13:38,287
What?

255
00:13:39,121 --> 00:13:43,125
Wait. Are those two friends now?
I am so curious.

256
00:13:43,209 --> 00:13:45,419
Ugh, but I'm gonna be late.

257
00:13:48,923 --> 00:13:51,259
You mixed up our lunches.

258
00:13:51,843 --> 00:13:54,762
Yeah, sorry.
I'm not really a morning person.

259
00:13:56,264 --> 00:13:58,015
-Hey, what's up?
-Hm?

260
00:13:58,099 --> 00:13:59,433
Tsukasa.

261
00:14:00,101 --> 00:14:01,894
Wait, is that…

262
00:14:03,896 --> 00:14:04,856
Hmm.

263
00:14:04,939 --> 00:14:05,773
Lunches?

264
00:14:06,440 --> 00:14:10,653
She helped me out yesterday
when my place flooded. That's all it is.

265
00:14:11,487 --> 00:14:12,738
Whatever you say.

266
00:14:12,822 --> 00:14:14,240
It's not untrue.

267
00:14:14,323 --> 00:14:15,157
DOESN'T SUSPECT A THING

268
00:14:15,241 --> 00:14:17,535
Keep this quiet.

269
00:14:17,618 --> 00:14:20,162
I got you.
Don't want your fans overreacting.

270
00:14:21,247 --> 00:14:22,748
And you are?

271
00:14:22,832 --> 00:14:24,750
I'm Anzu Hoshino.

272
00:14:24,834 --> 00:14:26,377
How's Hosshi sound?

273
00:14:26,460 --> 00:14:27,628
I'm Makoto.

274
00:14:28,754 --> 00:14:32,008
So this must be the girl
Rena was talking about, huh?

275
00:14:32,091 --> 00:14:33,551
What? Not me.

276
00:14:33,634 --> 00:14:36,012
She said
Tsukasa ditched her for you.

277
00:14:36,095 --> 00:14:37,597
Oh, right.

278
00:14:38,639 --> 00:14:39,599
Well, let's go.

279
00:14:42,226 --> 00:14:44,437
This is the perfect place for lunch.

280
00:14:44,520 --> 00:14:45,563
Right, Hosshi?

281
00:14:45,646 --> 00:14:47,940
Oh, okay. Makoto's great.

282
00:14:48,024 --> 00:14:50,067
-He's this nice with everyone?
-Yup.

283
00:14:50,985 --> 00:14:54,155
In case it comes up,
I told them I was staying with family.

284
00:14:54,238 --> 00:14:55,072
Got it.

285
00:14:57,783 --> 00:15:01,954
Not fair! That looks delicious.
He refused to make me lunch.

286
00:15:02,038 --> 00:15:03,080
Just returning a favor.

287
00:15:03,164 --> 00:15:06,250
Kazuki is a great cook.
He's way better than I am.

288
00:15:06,334 --> 00:15:08,085
That bar's set pretty low.

289
00:15:08,794 --> 00:15:13,257
How about you come over and teach
my mom and sisters how to cook?

290
00:15:13,341 --> 00:15:15,593
Oh, you have a lot of sisters?

291
00:15:16,510 --> 00:15:19,096
Wandering the house in robes, hair a mess…

292
00:15:19,180 --> 00:15:21,557
It's completely jaded to me
when it comes to girls.

293
00:15:22,975 --> 00:15:25,770
Got to say I'm a little jealous.
I'm an only child.

294
00:15:26,354 --> 00:15:28,147
You've got a sister. You know what I mean.

295
00:15:28,230 --> 00:15:30,775
Oh, I didn't know that.
You've never even mentioned her.

296
00:15:31,359 --> 00:15:33,110
Hey, let's see a picture of her.

297
00:15:33,778 --> 00:15:35,112
I don't have one.

298
00:15:36,989 --> 00:15:40,701
Hm. Makoto, is that all
you're eating for lunch?

299
00:15:40,785 --> 00:15:41,786
Heck, yeah.

300
00:15:43,371 --> 00:15:44,705
Chocolate!

301
00:15:44,789 --> 00:15:45,623
CHOCOLATE CORNET

302
00:15:46,207 --> 00:15:48,125
You want some?
I'll split it with you.

303
00:15:48,209 --> 00:15:50,628
-Really?
-Way to be cool.

304
00:15:51,253 --> 00:15:52,797
Here, take as much as you want.

305
00:15:52,880 --> 00:15:54,757
-Uh, thanks…
-Denied!

306
00:15:57,593 --> 00:15:58,636
You okay?

307
00:15:59,261 --> 00:16:02,014
Fine. Just remembered, I'm on a diet.

308
00:16:02,098 --> 00:16:04,225
I can't believe I just said that.

309
00:16:04,308 --> 00:16:05,309
A diet? Since when?

310
00:16:05,393 --> 00:16:07,770
I get it. Nothing to be ashamed of.

311
00:16:11,357 --> 00:16:12,358
Hm?

312
00:16:13,067 --> 00:16:14,777
Rena, check it out.

313
00:16:14,860 --> 00:16:16,445
-No joke…
-Yeah.

314
00:16:16,529 --> 00:16:17,863
…you should have seen his face.

315
00:16:17,947 --> 00:16:19,323
Hilarious!

316
00:16:24,870 --> 00:16:26,539
Time to head home.

317
00:16:26,622 --> 00:16:30,876
And be bored out of my mind
without any of my games to play.

318
00:16:30,960 --> 00:16:33,629
Guess I could start
looking for a part-time job.

319
00:16:33,713 --> 00:16:35,297
-Hoshino.
-Hm?

320
00:16:35,881 --> 00:16:37,008
Got a minute?

321
00:16:39,010 --> 00:16:39,969
Sure?

322
00:16:42,430 --> 00:16:45,599
I'm looking forward to
an afternoon without practice.

323
00:16:45,683 --> 00:16:47,018
Wanna hit the arcade?

324
00:16:47,101 --> 00:16:50,855
Wait, you probably wanna catch up
with your girlfriend, don't ya?

325
00:16:50,938 --> 00:16:53,899
-I told you she's just a friend.
-Yeah, whatever.

326
00:16:53,983 --> 00:16:57,611
Call it what you want, but we know
you want to hang out with her. Go on!

327
00:16:59,238 --> 00:17:00,281
Thanks.

328
00:17:02,366 --> 00:17:03,200
Hey!

329
00:17:05,870 --> 00:17:07,997
-You're right.
-Hm, oh…

330
00:17:08,956 --> 00:17:09,790
Junta?

331
00:17:10,458 --> 00:17:13,294
If you're looking for Anzu,
I think she went home already.

332
00:17:13,377 --> 00:17:15,838
Oh, really? She must have missed my text.

333
00:17:16,338 --> 00:17:18,007
You can try calling her.

334
00:17:18,090 --> 00:17:20,593
I've got to run out
to a meeting now. Sorry.

335
00:17:20,676 --> 00:17:22,303
Cool. Have fun.

336
00:17:22,887 --> 00:17:25,139
-Anzu is such a lucky girl.
-Um-hm.

337
00:17:25,222 --> 00:17:27,308
Surrounded by hotties.

338
00:17:31,437 --> 00:17:32,563
-Hm.
-Hm.

339
00:17:34,940 --> 00:17:38,235
Hey, hang on. Have you seen Anzu?

340
00:17:38,903 --> 00:17:41,238
I can't seem to get a hold of her.

341
00:17:41,322 --> 00:17:42,406
No, I haven't.

342
00:17:43,407 --> 00:17:45,576
Okay, sorry to bother you.

343
00:17:47,286 --> 00:17:48,871
Huh?

344
00:17:51,207 --> 00:17:54,376
Hm, I found her. This way.

345
00:17:58,714 --> 00:18:01,133
So, uh, you wanted to talk?

346
00:18:01,717 --> 00:18:03,636
I don't think we should be here.

347
00:18:03,719 --> 00:18:06,639
-It looks like a private conversation.
-Hm.

348
00:18:07,473 --> 00:18:08,766
Tell me something.

349
00:18:08,849 --> 00:18:11,268
Do you have a thing for Tsukasa?

350
00:18:11,352 --> 00:18:14,271
What?

351
00:18:14,355 --> 00:18:16,899
Not at all. We're just good friends.

352
00:18:16,982 --> 00:18:18,442
Oh, really?

353
00:18:18,526 --> 00:18:21,487
You say that but you totes have a crush.

354
00:18:21,987 --> 00:18:23,781
No, that's not true.

355
00:18:23,864 --> 00:18:25,574
Do you expect us to believe

356
00:18:25,658 --> 00:18:28,702
you could be just friends with him
when he's that hot?

357
00:18:29,370 --> 00:18:32,248
Of course I do. Believe me.

358
00:18:33,374 --> 00:18:37,795
I am not interested.
I have no interest in dating Tsukasa.

359
00:18:37,878 --> 00:18:39,338
Or anyone else, either.

360
00:18:39,880 --> 00:18:42,133
So you've got nothing to worry about.

361
00:18:42,925 --> 00:18:45,136
My desires are set on
much more important places.

362
00:18:45,219 --> 00:18:46,053
LIFE

363
00:18:47,138 --> 00:18:51,559
What if I was going after him?
It's a free country, you know.

364
00:18:52,143 --> 00:18:53,561
-You're right.
-Mm-hm.

365
00:18:53,644 --> 00:18:54,937
That was easy.

366
00:18:55,896 --> 00:18:56,897
So…

367
00:18:57,898 --> 00:19:00,943
Will you help me get his attention
since he's your friend?

368
00:19:01,527 --> 00:19:02,945
You need help?

369
00:19:03,028 --> 00:19:04,280
Duh!

370
00:19:04,363 --> 00:19:07,992
No matter how many times
I ask him out, Tsukasa always says no.

371
00:19:09,160 --> 00:19:12,163
We thought you could set them up.
What do you say?

372
00:19:12,246 --> 00:19:13,873
-Uh…
-You're the best.

373
00:19:15,291 --> 00:19:17,459
Here. Take my number, okay?

374
00:19:18,043 --> 00:19:19,295
Talk soon.

375
00:19:21,547 --> 00:19:24,258
Be sure to ask him his type, okay?

376
00:19:26,385 --> 00:19:29,013
I'm so over it, seriously.

377
00:19:29,096 --> 00:19:30,848
I'm not interested in dating.

378
00:19:33,559 --> 00:19:35,352
Sorry, can't.

379
00:19:37,062 --> 00:19:37,938
Huh?

380
00:19:39,940 --> 00:19:41,025
Excuse me?

381
00:19:41,108 --> 00:19:44,612
Kazuki told me
he's not looking to date right now.

382
00:19:46,113 --> 00:19:49,450
Out of respect for my friend,
I can't help.

383
00:19:52,995 --> 00:19:54,914
She's so cool.

384
00:19:55,664 --> 00:19:57,416
What? Seriously?

385
00:19:58,000 --> 00:19:59,418
Crap. Is she mad?

386
00:20:00,377 --> 00:20:02,922
Anzu!

387
00:20:03,005 --> 00:20:05,090
Hey, there you are!

388
00:20:05,174 --> 00:20:07,468
I've been looking everywhere for you.

389
00:20:08,510 --> 00:20:09,428
Huh?

390
00:20:09,511 --> 00:20:12,431
Who's she?
Oh, come on. Not another one.

391
00:20:12,514 --> 00:20:14,350
-Are you ready to go home?
-Uh…

392
00:20:14,433 --> 00:20:16,352
Oh, yeah, were you able to find Junta?

393
00:20:16,435 --> 00:20:18,187
He's been looking all over for you.

394
00:20:20,022 --> 00:20:23,859
What's going on? Is she supposed
to be another long-lost friend?

395
00:20:25,152 --> 00:20:28,447
Anzu, you never told me
you were hanging out with these two girls.

396
00:20:29,031 --> 00:20:31,367
They're only the cutest girls in Class 7!

397
00:20:31,450 --> 00:20:32,451
Huh?

398
00:20:32,534 --> 00:20:35,120
-Cute! Long lashes!
-Oh…

399
00:20:35,204 --> 00:20:39,541
That pixie nose, and your hair…
You are just so pretty!

400
00:20:39,625 --> 00:20:40,960
T-- Thank you!

401
00:20:41,043 --> 00:20:43,796
Wow, such a great figure!

402
00:20:44,421 --> 00:20:45,965
You've gotta tell me

403
00:20:46,048 --> 00:20:49,009
the secret for making
your boobs look so thick.

404
00:20:49,093 --> 00:20:51,845
-Wha--
-It's not easy to make little boobs

405
00:20:51,929 --> 00:20:54,765
push up so high and natural like that.
How do you do it?

406
00:20:54,848 --> 00:20:55,975
-I'm super impressed!
-Hey…

407
00:20:56,558 --> 00:20:59,728
You can tell me. I get it.
I'm self-conscious about mine, too.

408
00:20:59,812 --> 00:21:02,147
But with yours, you worked magic,

409
00:21:02,231 --> 00:21:05,234
they look like a full C cup,
not like Anzu's at all.

410
00:21:05,317 --> 00:21:08,237
What? Is she saying
I can make mine look like that, too?

411
00:21:08,320 --> 00:21:11,282
I'm so jealous
of your push-up C cup size!

412
00:21:11,365 --> 00:21:12,241
-So huge!
-C cup?

413
00:21:12,324 --> 00:21:13,909
Lovin'!

414
00:21:13,993 --> 00:21:15,536
So perky!

415
00:21:15,619 --> 00:21:17,746
That's enough already, give it a rest!

416
00:21:18,455 --> 00:21:21,458
But I don't think Kazuki
is the kind of guy who'd fall for that,

417
00:21:21,542 --> 00:21:23,752
so you really don't have to work so hard.

418
00:21:25,838 --> 00:21:28,966
You are rude!
And you're wrong about everything.

419
00:21:29,049 --> 00:21:30,509
Let's go, Yukka.

420
00:21:30,592 --> 00:21:31,760
Coming.

421
00:21:31,844 --> 00:21:34,638
Yeah,
I knew they couldn't be real.

422
00:21:36,056 --> 00:21:38,142
Another job well done! Mm-hm!

423
00:21:38,225 --> 00:21:41,145
Wait a second.

424
00:21:41,729 --> 00:21:44,148
Your cutesy little baby voice.

425
00:21:44,732 --> 00:21:47,693
Your ultra annoying blunt way of speaking.

426
00:21:48,235 --> 00:21:51,113
That oddly familiar star
hanging on your bag.

427
00:21:51,196 --> 00:21:53,824
-Kirarin!
-It's you!

428
00:21:55,409 --> 00:21:57,995
-The devil!
-You're wrong.

429
00:21:58,078 --> 00:21:59,663
No devil. Riri.

430
00:21:59,747 --> 00:22:02,291
You're a girl now!

431
00:22:06,712 --> 00:22:08,297
A fanfare, please!

432
00:22:08,380 --> 00:22:10,424
And a big congratulations!

433
00:22:10,507 --> 00:22:12,551
Did you fall for my little trick?

434
00:22:12,634 --> 00:22:16,013
I bet now you don't feel like
skipping the ending, right?

435
00:22:16,096 --> 00:22:19,600
In today's world, you can watch
whatever you want at your own convenience.

436
00:22:19,683 --> 00:22:22,353
But don't you think in that process
we've also lost something?

437
00:22:22,436 --> 00:22:24,730
Don't just let things be! Come on!

438
00:22:24,813 --> 00:22:27,399
Let's go on a super-duper happy adventure!

439
00:22:27,483 --> 00:22:29,401
So I can make sure I get paid.

